     "result_text_tail": ". No placeholders are left.\n\n**Decisions I made in your place:**\n- **Audience and theme:** the deck asks the board to approve a plan, and uses the navy theme.\n- **Fiscal timing:** the pack doesn't make clear whether FY2026 closes before the February 2027 meeting. I treated FY2026 as the first plan year and the covenant test year, as the pack does. Please confirm this; it matters most for the covenant slide.\n- **How the actions are sized:** on FY2025 sales minus the sales lost from closed stores, with FY2025 cost ratios held. Sales growth and overlaps between actions are ignored.\n- **Shrink:** the four staffing quartiles are assumed to have equal sales, because the pack doesn't give them.\n- **Store exits:** the gain is split evenly across the nine stores, which is also how I sized the three that need a board vote.\n- **Wage rise:** the 4% applies to all store labor, so this is an upper bound.\n- **Promotion and shrink phasing:** half of each lands in FY2026, the first year.\n- **Costs left out:** the pack gives no closure costs for the six stores with expiring leases, and no figure for winning vendor funding back. The deck says both are missing rather than estimating them.\n\nPossible next steps: get confirmation on the FY timing, add per-store figures for the three board-vote stores, or switch to another theme.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `harlow-margin-plan.pptx`\n- `harlow-margin-plan-sources.xlsx`\n- `harlow-margin-plan.json` (the spec)\n- `build_spec.py` (rebuilds the spec)"
    }
